# Windows batch files must keep CRLF, and must keep it *in the stored blob* —
# not just in the working tree. `text eol=crlf` would store LF and convert on
# checkout, which is fine for a clone but wrong for the main way people get this
# file: GitHub's "download raw file" button serves the blob verbatim, so a
# normalised .bat arrives LF-only. cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files —
# goto/call label seeking is the usual casualty, and Install-Orca-Plugins.bat is
# built almost entirely out of labels.
#
# `-text` disables EOL conversion in both directions; `diff` forces git to still
# treat them as text so changes stay reviewable.
*.bat -text diff
*.cmd -text diff
*.ps1 -text diff

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
